; What a stage reports when it refuses its input, and the rendering of that
; report for a person at a terminal.
;
; Below the compiler stages for the same reason `source` is: a diagnostic
; points at source, and every stage from the parser on has something to
; refuse. The structure is what a stage hands back -- a caller can read its
; span and severity, sort, filter, or serialise it -- and `Render` is one way
; of printing it, applied by whichever binary decides the text is for a human.
(library
 (name diagnostic)
 (libraries source))
